# The names the public repository must never carry (CONTRIBUTING.md,
# "Editorial rule"), as the SHA-256 of the lower-case name, so that this list
# does not name them either. A name is one word, or two or three words written
# together or joined by one space (ASCII letters and digits only), 4 to 24
# characters long: the digest of "quux cad" or "quuxcad". To add one:
#   printf 'quuxcad' | shasum -a 256
# The one list of the rule: test/editorial_names_test.dart checks the whole
# repository with it, and the pre-commit hook (tool/hooks/pre-commit,
# tool/hooks/banned_names.dart) the lines a commit adds, every name of both
# sections in every file; the hook also reads the plain local list
# <git dir>/info/banned-words, which is never committed.

